<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Inverse of Polynomials — inverse of a linear function</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Let \( f(x) = {@fx@} \).</p>
<p>Find \( f^{-1}(x) \), giving your answer in terms of \(x\).</p>
<div>\( f^{-1}(x) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The <strong>inverse function</strong> \(f^{-1}\) undoes \(f\): it takes each output of \(f\) back to the input that produced it. To find it, write \(y = f(x)\), swap the roles of \(x\) and \(y\), and make \(y\) the subject.</p>
\[
\begin{align*}
x &= {@fy@}\\
{@x-b@} &= {@m*y@}\\
y &= {@ta@}
\end{align*}
\]
<p>So \(f^{-1}(x) = {@ta@}\). The whole of \({@x-b@}\) is divided by \({@m@}\), not just the \(x\). Check: \(f\big(f^{-1}(x)\big) = {@m@}\left({@ta@}\right) [[if test="is(b>0)"]]+ {@b@}[[else]]- {@-b@}[[/if]] = x\).</p>
<p>The graph of \(f^{-1}\) is the reflection of the graph of \(f\) in the line \(y = x\), because swapping \(x\) and \(y\) swaps the coordinates of every point.</p>
<div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="The line y = f(x), its inverse y = f inverse of x, and the dashed mirror line y = x.">
[[jsxgraph width="320px" height="320px"]]
(function() {
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {
    boundingbox: [-10, 10, 10, -10], axis: true, grid: false,
    showNavigation: false, showCopyright: false
  });
  b.create('functiongraph', [function(x){ return {#m#}*x + {#b#}; }], {strokeColor:'#003399', strokeWidth:2});
  b.create('functiongraph', [function(x){ return (x - ({#b#}))/({#m#}); }], {strokeColor:'#cc0000', strokeWidth:2});
  b.create('functiongraph', [function(x){ return x; }], {strokeColor:'#666666', dash:2, strokeWidth:1});
  b.create('text', [-9.5, 9, 'blue: y = f(x)'], {fixed:true, color:'#003399'});
  b.create('text', [-9.5, 7.8, 'red: y = f⁻¹(x)'], {fixed:true, color:'#cc0000'});
  b.create('text', [-9.5, 6.6, 'dashed: y = x'], {fixed:true, color:'#666666'});
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
